ok   change records operations in call order
ok   add_reference records an add_reference operation and, by default, an add_foreign_key operation
ok   add_reference(foreign_key: false) records only the add_reference operation
ok   add_foreign_key defaults its column to singularize(to_table) + _id
ok   add_reference and add_foreign_key inflect irregular and compound names through Cybertrain::Inflector
ok   inverse of create_table is drop_table
ok   inverse of add_column is remove_column
ok   inverse of add_index is remove_index
ok   inverse of rename_column reverses the direction
ok   inverse raises IrreversibleMigration for a kind with no automatic down
ok   register/all order migrations by version regardless of registration order
ok   self.version / self.version_string are per-subclass
ok   up resets operations, so calling it twice does not duplicate them
ok   down on a change-only migration replays the inverse operations in reverse order
ok   down resets operations, so calling it twice does not duplicate them
ok   down raises IrreversibleMigration when change recorded a non-invertible operation
ok   add_index accepts Symbol columns
ok   add_index name: overrides the derived name, for symmetry with Definition#add_index
ok   add_column takes precision: and scale: for a decimal
ok   add_index takes where: for a partial index
ok   add_reference and add_foreign_key take on_delete:
ok   a create_table recorded by a migration writes DECIMAL(p,s) and ON DELETE RESTRICT
ok   add_column raises ArgumentError for a scale without a precision
ok   add_reference raises ArgumentError for on_delete: :nullify on a NOT NULL column
ok   add_reference with Symbol arguments folds its foreign key into the ADD COLUMN
ok   the new kinds record one Operation each, with the fields they reuse
ok   change_column_default without from: is recorded as not knowing the previous default
ok   change_column_null without a default backfills nothing
ok   inverse of rename_table swaps the names
ok   inverse of change_column_default with from: and to: swaps them
ok   inverse of change_column_null flips null when the previous state can be restored
ok   change_column, remove_reference and remove_foreign_key have no automatic inverse
ok   reversible records the up block as :reversible_up and the down block as :reversible_down
ok   reversible's blocks take only execute
ok   rebuild_table copies the common columns through <table>_new and restores indexes, triggers and the sequence
ok   table_after applies each rebuild kind to a copy of the table
36 tests, 158 assertions, 0 failures
